Input: {"question": "Who is Catharina Six's spouse?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 87, "text": "**Breaking News: Uncovering the Hidden Marriage of Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 89, "end": 338, "text": "Amsterdam, Netherlands - In a stunning revelation, our investigative team has uncovered conclusive evidence that Catharina Six, the renowned Dutch art collector, was married to Jan Bernd Bicker, a prominent Dutch politician of the Batavian Republic."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 339, "end": 563, "text": "According to historical records and expert testimony, Catharina Six, born in 1752, and Jan Bernd Bicker, born in 1746, tied the knot in a private ceremony, solidifying their union and cementing their places in Dutch history."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 564, "end": 567, "text": "Dr."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 568, "end": 835, "text": "Maria van der Meer, a leading historian at the University of Amsterdam, confirmed the marriage, stating, \"After conducting an exhaustive review of archival documents and correspondence, it is clear that Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker were indeed husband and wife."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 836, "end": 931, "text": "Their marriage was a significant union, bringing together two influential figures of the time.\""}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 932, "end": 1038, "text": "Catharina Six, known for her exquisite taste in art, was a prominent figure in Amsterdam's cultural scene."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1039, "end": 1217, "text": "Her marriage to Jan Bernd Bicker, a member of the Batavian Republic's Staatsbewind from 1803 to 1805, highlights the intersection of art and politics in 18th-century Netherlands."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1218, "end": 1407, "text": "\"The marriage between Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker is a fascinating example of the complex relationships between art, politics, and society during the Batavian Republic era,\" said Dr."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1408, "end": 1465, "text": "Pieter van der Velden, a specialist in Dutch art history."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1466, "end": 1599, "text": "\"Their union underscores the significant role that women like Catharina played in shaping the cultural landscape of the Netherlands.\""}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1600, "end": 1670, "text": "Our investigation uncovered several key pieces of evidence, including:"}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1672, "end": 1674, "text": "1."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1675, "end": 1864, "text": "**Marriage records**: Archival documents from the Amsterdam City Archives confirm the marriage between Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker, with the exact date of the ceremony still unknown."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1865, "end": 1867, "text": "2."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1868, "end": 2039, "text": "**Correspondence**: Letters exchanged between Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker, housed at the Rijksmuseum, reveal a deep affection and mutual respect between the couple."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2040, "end": 2042, "text": "3."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2043, "end": 2210, "text": "**Testimonies**: Eyewitness accounts from contemporaries, including artists and politicians, corroborate the marriage, providing a rich tapestry of historical context."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2211, "end": 2400, "text": "In conclusion, our investigation has established beyond a reasonable doubt that Catharina Six, the esteemed art collector, was married to Jan Bernd Bicker, the influential Dutch politician."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 129, "text": "As I wandered through the labyrinthine corridors of the Rijksmuseum, I stumbled upon a peculiar exhibit that caught my attention."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 130, "end": 239, "text": "Amidst the masterpieces of the Dutch Golden Age, a small, unassuming portrait of a woman seemed out of place."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 240, "end": 375, "text": "Her piercing green eyes and raven-black hair were a stark contrast to the soft, golden light that illuminated the surrounding artworks."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 376, "end": 443, "text": "The placard read: \"Catharina Six, Dutch art collector (1752-1793)\"."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 444, "end": 555, "text": "I couldn't help but feel drawn to her enigmatic smile, as if she held secrets beyond the confines of her frame."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 556, "end": 638, "text": "As I gazed deeper, a faint whisper seemed to echo through the gallery, \"Alison...\""}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 639, "end": 694, "text": "The sound was so soft, I wondered if I had imagined it."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 695, "end": 751, "text": "Suddenly, a gentle touch on my shoulder broke the spell."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 752, "end": 821, "text": "I turned to face a woman with an uncanny resemblance to the portrait."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 822, "end": 882, "text": "Her eyes, though not as piercing, shared the same intensity."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 883, "end": 971, "text": "Her dark hair, now flecked with wisps of silver, was styled in a modern, effortless bob."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 972, "end": 1038, "text": "\"Lost in thought, I see,\" she said, her voice husky and confident."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1039, "end": 1085, "text": "\"Catharina Six was a true pioneer in her time."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1086, "end": 1146, "text": "Her passion for art rivaled that of the masters themselves.\""}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1147, "end": 1217, "text": "I introduced myself, and she replied, \"I'm Alison Catherine MacGregor."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1218, "end": 1272, "text": "I've spent years studying Catharina's life and legacy."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1273, "end": 1332, "text": "There's something about her that resonates deeply with me.\""}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1333, "end": 1422, "text": "As we strolled through the museum, Alison's knowledge of Catharina's life was staggering."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1423, "end": 1562, "text": "She spoke of the art collector's fierce determination, her unwavering support for emerging artists, and her unrelenting passion for beauty."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1563, "end": 1673, "text": "With each step, I sensed an unspoken connection between the two women, a bond that transcended time and space."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1674, "end": 1812, "text": "As we paused before a stunning Vermeer, Alison's eyes locked onto mine, and for an instant, I saw a flicker of Catharina's piercing green."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1813, "end": 1903, "text": "It was as if the art collector's spirit had awakened, bridging the centuries between them."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1904, "end": 1991, "text": "\"Tell me, Alison,\" I asked, my curiosity piqued, \"what draws you to Catharina's story?\""}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1992, "end": 2074, "text": "Alison's smile was enigmatic, much like the portrait that had first captivated me."}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2075, "end": 2163, "text": "\"Perhaps it's the sense of kindred spirits,\" she said, her voice barely above a whisper."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Jan Bernd Bicker", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Jan Bernd Bicker", "scope": "Spouse of Catharina Six", "claim": "Catharina Six was married to Jan Bernd Bicker, a prominent Dutch politician of the Batavian Republic.", "answer": "Jan Bernd Bicker", "quote": "Amsterdam, Netherlands - In a stunning revelation, our investigative team has uncovered conclusive evidence that Catharina Six, the renowned Dutch art collector, was married to Jan Bernd Bicker, a prominent Dutch politician of the Batavian Republic. According to historical records and expert testimony, Catharina Six, born in 1752, and Jan Bernd Bicker, born in 1746, tied the knot in a private ceremony, solidifying their union and cementing their places in Dutch history. Dr. Maria van der Meer, a leading historian at the University of Amsterdam, confirmed the marriage, stating, \"After conducting an exhaustive review of archival documents and correspondence, it is clear that Catharina Six and Jan Bernd Bicker were indeed husband and wife. Their marriage was a significant union, bringing together two influential figures of the time.\" Catharina Six, known for her exquisite taste in art, was a prominent figure in Amsterdam's cultural scene. Her marriage to Jan Bernd Bicker, a member of the Batavian Republic's Staatsbewind from 1803 to 1805, highlights the intersection of art and politics in 18th-century Netherlands.", "original_document_number"